@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title The scope page and the filter list — a folder tree with the root first, and one list for every other pick
' purpose: how a monorepo run asks where the agent works, and what replaced the three go-fuzzyfinder pickers
' covers: internal/choiceui/tree.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/tree_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/scope_page.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/scope_page_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/filter_list.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/filter_list_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go (pickProject, scopePage, scopePageAnswer)
' covers: cmd/proveo/running.go (pickIndex, offer)
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/maintain.go (listPickTargets, targetsAt)
' covers: e2e/target_list_test.go
'   the decision, D6 ................. _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (DECISIONS, W10)
'   when a run shows the page ........ _spec/internal/run/run-spec.puml
'   the stack it draws with .......... _spec/internal/choiceui/tui-stack.puml
'   the key line it shares ........... _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT IT REPLACES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' go-fuzzyfinder had three call sites: the monorepo scope (a flat list under
' "scope> "), the run and attach list, and proveo-dev's multi-select. The
' scope list did not mark the root as the default, and it was a different
' program from the form, so the choice could not be revisited.
' The Executor, D6: "Every run, Enter keeps root". Not chosen: the page on
' the first run only, with a per-repo memory; a scope row inside the form,
' which would have needed no page loop.
'
' ── THE TREE IS A PURE MODEL (W-c) ─────────────────────────────────────────
' Tree (tree.go) holds folders, folds, a filter and a cursor. It imports no
' terminal library, so every rule below is a unit test.
'   THE ROOT IS ROW 0 AND THE CURSOR STARTS ON IT. Enter alone keeps the
'   answer a run took before the page existed.
'   FOLDERS DERIVE FROM THE PROJECT PATHS. NewTree takes each
'   workspace.Project.Path and adds every folder above it. Siblings sort by
'   name.
'   FOLD closes the cursor's folder. On a closed folder or a leaf it steps to
'   the folder above, so one key walks up the tree. The root never folds.
'   A FILTER KEEPS THE ROOT. It shows the paths that hold the text, and the
'   folders above them, and sees through folds. The cursor goes to the first
'   match unless it is on one; with no match it returns to the root.
'   MEASURED: the first version kept the cursor on the root under a filter,
'   so "/worker" then Enter chose the root. A unit test caught it.
'   Clearing the filter keeps the cursor and opens the folders above it.
'   PLACE puts the cursor on a path and opens what hides it. A step back from
'   the form uses it, so the page reopens where it was left.
'   HOLDS reports whether a path lies below the cursor's folder. The root
'   holds every other path; a folder does not hold itself; "app" does not
'   hold "apps/web". The page's cyan guides read it.
' NOT A TOOL COLUMN: internal/workspace/discover.go gives every project in a
' repository the same Tool.
' EVERY FOLDER IS A SCOPE, NOT ONLY A PROJECT. The old list offered the root
' and the projects. The tree also offers the folders between: `apps` when
' the projects are `apps/web` and `apps/api`.
' [Inference] That is safe because --scope already takes any path under the
' repository and the run joins it to the root unchecked. No run was started
' from a folder that is not a project.
'
' ── THE PAGE (W-f) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' ScopePage (scope_page.go) is a Bubble Tea model over the tree. It draws
' through the same screen, canvas and pen as the form.
'   the banner            when the terminal holds it and the whole tree
'   the title             "run <target> — where the agent works", and a chip
'                         "scope · 1/2" at the right when it is one of two
'   "/ <text>"            only while a filter is open or set
'   the tree              a window that follows the cursor
'   one sentence          where Enter starts the agent
'   the key line          two-tone, narrowed by KEEP rank like the form's
' A leaf's name starts in the column a sibling folder's fold mark does.
' MEASURED: with the name one step further right, `tools` read as a child of
' the folder above it.
' GUIDES (2026-11-11). A row draws one guide per folder above it, under that
' folder's fold mark; the root's guide is column 2. A guide inside the
' cursor's folder is brand cyan; every other guide is ColorRule grey. The
' cyan region is what the agent gets: on the root row every guide is cyan.
' Under the ASCII and Off glyph tiers a guide is |.
' The window scrolls ahead to the last row the cursor's folder holds, as far
' as the cursor stays on screen. MEASURED by review: at 60x12, six downs left
' "services" on the bottom row with billing and worker, and their cyan
' guides, below the window.
' The operator: "a cyan line should highlight what it contains for
' visibility; lines should be shown for subfolders too", then chose the
' cyan region over two proposals. NOT CHOSEN: cyan lines under the cursor's
' folder with no grey guides elsewhere; one cyan guide for the cursor's own
' folder with its subfolders' guides grey (VS Code's indent guides).
' The root row reads "<repository>  repo root  default".
' A folded folder says how many given paths it hides: "2 inside".
' The fold marks are U+25BE and U+25B8; under the ASCII glyph tier, - and +.
' THE ENTER WORD IS "choose", NOT "accept". e2e's acceptChoicePrompt waits
' for "enter accept" and presses Enter; on this page that would take the root
' without anyone reading the tree. A unit test and an e2e both refuse the
' string on this page.
' KEYS. ↑↓ PgUp PgDn Home End move. ← folds, → opens. "/" opens the filter;
' typing then narrows, Backspace on an empty filter closes it, Esc clears it.
' Enter chooses the cursor's row. Esc with no filter cancels. Ctrl+C asks
' first when the page is one of two (_spec/internal/choiceui/wizard-keys.puml).
' Esc means two things here on purpose: clear, then cancel.
' UNDER ITS FLOOR (7 rows, 8 with a filter) the page says so, names what
' Enter keeps, and takes only Enter, Esc and Ctrl+C.
' Golden frames: internal/choiceui/testdata/scope/, 24 files (six states at
' four sizes).
'
' ── THE FILTER LIST (B8) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
' FilterList (filter_list.go) is the one list for the other two pickers.
' Typing narrows at once, as the finder did. Enter takes the cursor's row.
' With Multi, Tab marks a row and moves down; Enter takes every marked row
' in list order, or the cursor's row when none is marked.
' A ROW MATCHES WHEN IT HOLDS EVERY TYPED WORD, case ignored. The finder
' matched a subsequence of letters; this is stricter.
' [Inference] No operator relied on subsequence matching for lists of about
' ten harness names. Nobody was asked.
' A mark survives a filter that hides its row.
' Under its floor the list only cancels: Enter must not choose a row nobody
' can see.
' Pick() returns ErrListClosed for Esc, so each caller words its own refusal:
' "no target selected", "no task selected". Since R4 `proveo attach` prints
' its own "⚠ attach — no task selected" (exit 1, the operator's choice); `proveo
' run` and the harness aliases still end on main's ×.
' proveo-dev's row 0 is "all": alone or among others it means every target.
' Golden frames: internal/choiceui/testdata/list/, 9 files.
'
' ── THE LIBRARIES LEFT (B9) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' go.mod lost tcell, go-fuzzyfinder and the four modules only they required:
' gdamore/encoding, go-ansisgr, termbox-go and pkg/errors. go.sum lost 13
' lines. The lines were removed by hand: `go mod tidy` would also drop
' martian, x/net, x/text and the bubbles pin, which this change does not own.
' A contract test reads every import and go.mod for the three library names.
'
' ── WHAT RAN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' macOS, tmux: the scope page opens, Esc cancels with status 1; three rows
' down and Enter opens the form as page 2/2; shift+tab returns to the page on
' the same row; Home and Enter reopen the form; Esc ends the run and no
' scope line prints. A bare `proveo run` lists its targets, narrows on
' typing and ends with "no target selected" on Esc.
' linux/arm64, tmux: the list test passed twice. The two scope tests SKIP
' there: the container has no sbx, and the run refuses before the page.
' NOT RUN: proveo-dev's multi-select on a terminal. Its mapping is unit
' tested; the list it uses is the one the tmux test drives.
'
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/tree_test.go:
'   TestTheRootIsTheFirstRowAndTheCursorStartsOnIt
'   TestFoldingHidesAFoldersRowsAndCountsThem
'   TestFoldOnALeafOrAClosedFolderStepsToTheFolderAbove
'   TestPlaceOpensTheFoldersAboveAndRefusesAnUnknownPath
'   TestTheCursorsFolderHoldsEveryPathBelowItAndTheRootHoldsAll
'   TestAFilterKeepsTheRootTheMatchesAndTheFoldersAboveThem
'   TestAFilterPutsTheCursorOnItsFirstMatch
'   TestClearingAFilterKeepsTheCursorAndOpensTheFoldersAboveIt
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/scope_page_test.go:
'   TestEnterAloneKeepsTheRepoRoot
'   TestTheScopePagesKeys
'   TestTheRootRowIsMarkedDefaultAndTheLineUnderTheTreeFollowsTheCursor
'   TestAShortTerminalScrollsTheTreeAndKeepsTheCursorAndTheFoot
'   TestBelowItsFloorTheScopePageSaysSoAndStillLeaves
'   TestTheGuidesInsideTheCursorsFolderAreBrandAndTheRestAreRuleGrey
'   TestMovingDownOntoAFolderScrollsItsContentsIntoTheWindow
'   TestTheScopePageMatchesItsGoldenFrames
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/filter_list_test.go:
'   TestTheFilterListsKeys
'   TestAShortTerminalScrollsTheListAndATinyOneOnlyCancels
'   TestTheFilterListMatchesItsGoldenFrames
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/main_test.go:
'   TestAClosedScopePageCancelsAndAPageThatCannotDrawKeepsTheRepoRoot
'   TestTheScopePageOpensOnTheRepoRootOrWhereAnEarlierVisitLeftIt
' Pinned by cmd/proveo-dev/maintain_test.go:
'   TestTheAllRowAloneOrAmongOthersIsEveryTarget
' Pinned by internal/contract/tui_ratchets_test.go:
'   TestTheRetiredTUILibrariesStayOut
' Pinned by e2e: TestEscInTheScopePageCancelsTheRun,
'   TestTheFormStepsBackToTheScopePageWhereItWasLeft,
'   TestABareRunListsItsTargetsNarrowsOnTypingAndCancelsOnEsc

component "project paths\nworkspace.DiscoverProjects" as PROJ <<data>>
component "Tree\nfolds · filter · cursor" as TREE <<app>>
component "the root row\nrow 0 · default · the cursor starts here" as ROOT <<host>>
component "ScopePage\npage 1 of a monorepo run" as PAGE <<app>>
component "the form\npage 2 · shift+tab steps back" as FORM <<app>>
component "FilterList\nrun · attach · proveo-dev targets" as LIST <<app>>
component "go-fuzzyfinder · tcell\n**gone from go.mod**" as GONE <<error>>

PROJ ARROW_MAIN TREE : every folder above each path
TREE ARROW_MAIN ROOT
TREE ARROW_MAIN PAGE
PAGE ARROW_MAIN FORM : Enter
FORM ARROW_OPTIONAL PAGE : a step back, same row
GONE ARROW_ERROR PAGE : replaced by
GONE ARROW_ERROR LIST : replaced by

note bottom of ROOT
  **Enter alone keeps the old answer.** The
  root is the first row, marked default, and
  the cursor starts on it. A run that only
  presses Enter works on the whole repository.
end note

note bottom of TREE
  **A filter moves the cursor to its match.**
  The root stays on screen under a filter. A
  cursor left on it would make "/web" then
  Enter choose the root.
end note

note right of PAGE
  **Cyan is what the agent gets.** Every open
  folder draws a grey guide; the guides inside
  the cursor's folder turn cyan, the guides of
  its subfolders too.
end note

note bottom of PAGE
  **It never says "enter accept".** The e2e
  helpers wait for those words and press
  Enter. Here that would take the root, so
  the page says "enter choose".
end note

note bottom of FORM
  **A step back keeps both pages.** The scope
  page reopens on the row it was left on, and
  the form gets its earlier answers back where
  the options are the same.
end note

note bottom of LIST
  **Every typed word must be in the row.** The
  finder matched a subsequence of letters. A
  list of harness names needs less, and a
  stricter match is easier to predict.
end note

note bottom of GONE
  **Removed by hand, not by tidy.** A tidy
  would also drop four lines this change does
  not own. A contract test now fails on any
  import or go.mod line that names them.
end note
@enduml
